%% DM26-0670

%% How an agent catches up with the credentials agent's authority, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/authority-distribution.md, "Snapshots", "Pruning the
%% revoked set", "Pinning the key to the CA"). How an update starts is general/policy_update_enforcement, and what a revoked serial does is general/revocation.
%% The same core (AuthorityCore) runs in every builder agent, in the broker and in each custody daemon's custodian session.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Pub as credentials agent<br/>(publisher)
    participant Ledger as credentials agent<br/>(ledger)
    participant Bk as Cassini broker
    participant Leaf as a leaf: agent, broker or daemon<br/>(AuthorityCore)
    participant CI as cert-issuer

    Note over CI,Pub: The key it signs with is its escrow key. Nothing<br/>certifies a key made in its own pod, so it asks
    Pub->>CI: /internal/issue, a Signing certificate for its own identity, a CSR made with that key
    CI-->>Pub: the certificate. Renewed at half its life,<br/>tried again every few seconds while cert-issuer cannot answer
    Note over Pub: No snapshot goes out before this one, and one goes out at once when it comes

    Note over Bk,Leaf: When a leaf asks
    alt its Cassini client registers, or registers again
        Leaf-)Bk: AuthoritySnapshotRequest on polar-authority-snapshot-requests
    else it has no key pinned, every 30 s
        Leaf-)Bk: the same
    else an update shows a jump in the sequence, at most once in 5 s
        Leaf-)Bk: the same
    else the broker refused what its own gate let through: it may be behind
        Leaf-)Bk: the same
    else it is the broker, once at its start, which never registers
        Note over Bk: Asks as a leaf. It waits on the topic until the credentials agent subscribes
    end

    Bk-)Pub: the request
    alt no snapshot in the last 5 s
        Pub-)Bk: the snapshot on polar-authority-snapshot-replies
    else one went out a moment ago, perhaps before this asker was listening
        Pub->>Pub: one more when the 5 s end, for everyone who asked in them. None is dropped
        Pub-)Bk: the snapshot
    end
    Note over Pub,Bk: It also republishes after half an hour with no update (REPUBLISH_AFTER), the backstop for one that missed it

    Bk-)Leaf: the snapshot, to every subscriber, stamped with who published it
    Note over Leaf: The key, the key's certificate chain, and<br/>the latest signed update of each kind:<br/>a bundle of signed updates, not a document signed whole

    Leaf->>Leaf: published by the credentials agent's identity, or ignored:<br/>checked first, so nobody else causes signature work
    Leaf->>Leaf: the chain goes to its pinned CA, is valid now,<br/>names that identity, carries id-kp-documentSigning,<br/>and is for the key the snapshot names.<br/>Otherwise nothing is believed
    alt no key pinned yet
        Leaf->>Leaf: pin it, for good
    else it is another key, certified or not
        Leaf->>Leaf: refused and reported: a key that changes<br/>is an incident, never an update
    end
    loop each update in it
        Leaf->>Leaf: verify on its own. One that fails is skipped<br/>and reported, and the rest apply
        Leaf->>Leaf: a higher version replaces what is<br/>held. A jump here is not a miss
    end
    Leaf->>Leaf: policy, groups, revoked serials: to the actors<br/>that hold them, and AuthorityChanged

    Note over Pub,Ledger: The revoked set only grows in the ledger. What is published does not, or every leaf would look through a set that grows with each restart
    loop every 10 minutes, and on each revocation
        Pub->>Ledger: PublishedRevocations
        Ledger-->>Pub: the set, less serials whose certificate ended more than 2 hours ago,<br/>and a version: ever revoked plus ended, which never falls
        opt the version rose
            Pub-)Bk: the signed Revoked update on polar-authority-updates
            Bk-)Leaf: delivered. A smaller set with a higher version replaces the larger
        end
    end
